WEBVTT

00:03.718 --> 00:04.886
KATARA: Water...

00:04.969 --> 00:06.888
Earth...

00:07.013 --> 00:08.890
Fire...

00:09.015 --> 00:11.434
Air.

00:11.559 --> 00:12.852
Long ago...

00:12.977 --> 00:14.938
The four nations lived
together in harmony.

00:15.063 --> 00:19.984
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:20.109 --> 00:23.988
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements could stop them.

00:24.113 --> 00:25.782
But when the world
needed him most

00:25.907 --> 00:27.992
he vanished.

00:28.117 --> 00:31.496
100 years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

00:31.621 --> 00:33.456
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.581 --> 00:35.875
And although his airbending
skills were great

00:36.000 --> 00:37.877
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.961 --> 00:39.045
AANG: Oof.

00:39.212 --> 00:43.091
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

00:43.216 --> 00:45.385
( ♪... )

00:48.012 --> 00:50.348
( MAN READING )

00:51.224 --> 00:53.393
OZAI: I am proud of you,
prince Zuko.

00:53.476 --> 00:56.729
I am proud because when your
loyalty was tested

00:56.854 --> 00:58.982
by your treacherous uncle

00:59.107 --> 01:00.483
you did the right thing

01:00.608 --> 01:02.235
and captured the traitor.

01:02.360 --> 01:05.863
ZUKO: Why did you tell Father
that I was the one who killed the Avatar?

01:05.989 --> 01:07.407
Please, Zuko...

01:07.532 --> 01:09.617
What ulterior motive
could I have

01:09.701 --> 01:13.913
Unless somehow the Avatar
was actually alive?

01:13.997 --> 01:15.832
All that glory would
suddenly turn to shame.

01:18.876 --> 01:21.754
( ♪... )

01:59.000 --> 02:00.001
Who's there?

02:08.801 --> 02:12.639
( WIND HOWLING )

02:12.722 --> 02:14.432
AANG: I think I see
a cave below.

02:14.515 --> 02:17.143
SOKKA: Shh... Keep quiet.

02:20.188 --> 02:21.856
( BIRD SQUAWKS )

02:21.981 --> 02:23.107
( APPA GRUNTS )

02:23.232 --> 02:26.235
Great job with the cloud camo,
but next time...

02:26.319 --> 02:28.071
Let's disguise ourselves as
the kind of cloud

02:28.154 --> 02:30.156
who knows how to keep its mouth shut.

02:30.698 --> 02:34.369
TOPH: Yeah, we wouldn't want a bird to
hear us chatting up there and turn us in.

02:34.494 --> 02:37.080
Hey, we're in enemy territory.

02:37.205 --> 02:39.624
Those are enemy birds.

02:39.749 --> 02:41.584
( SQUAWK )

02:41.709 --> 02:43.586
( CHUCKLING )

02:47.340 --> 02:48.383
( CRASHES )

02:55.056 --> 02:56.641
SOKKA: Well, this is it.

02:56.724 --> 02:58.935
This is how we'll be living
until the invasion begins.

02:59.018 --> 03:01.562
Hiding in cave after cave...

03:01.646 --> 03:04.440
After cave after cave...

03:04.649 --> 03:07.735
Sokka, we don't need
to become cave people.

03:07.819 --> 03:09.946
What we need
is some new clothes.

03:10.029 --> 03:12.490
Yeah, blending in
is better than hiding out.

03:12.573 --> 03:14.242
If we get Fire Nation disguises

03:14.325 --> 03:17.620
we'll be just as safe as we
would be hiding in a cave.

03:17.704 --> 03:19.330
Plus, they have
real food out there.

03:19.414 --> 03:21.582
Does anyone wanna sit in the
dirt and eat cave-hoppers?

03:27.088 --> 03:29.465
( CRUNCHING )

03:29.882 --> 03:32.802
Looks like we
got outvoted, sport.

03:32.885 --> 03:34.345
Let's get some new clothes.

03:36.723 --> 03:38.099
AANG: I don't know about this.

03:38.182 --> 03:39.684
These clothes
belong to somebody.

03:39.767 --> 03:42.311
I call the silk robe.

03:44.981 --> 03:47.358
But if it's essential
to our survival

03:47.442 --> 03:49.610
then I call the suit.

04:02.540 --> 04:04.333
Ta-dah... Normal kid.

04:04.751 --> 04:07.920
Hmm... I should
probably wear shoes

04:08.004 --> 04:10.590
But then I won't
be able to see as well.

04:10.923 --> 04:12.759
Sorry shoes...

04:15.511 --> 04:19.932
Finally, a stylish shoe
for the blind earthbender.

04:20.016 --> 04:21.392
How do I look?

04:25.855 --> 04:28.065
Uh, your mom's necklace.

04:28.191 --> 04:30.943
Oh... Oh, yeah.

04:31.068 --> 04:33.404
I guess it's pretty obviously
Water Tribe, isn't it?

04:46.501 --> 04:47.752
( MOMO PURRS )

04:50.338 --> 04:53.800
I used to visit my friend
Kuzon here 100 years ago.

04:53.883 --> 04:56.427
So everyone just follow
my lead and stay cool.

04:56.511 --> 04:58.304
Or as they say
in the Fire Nation

04:58.387 --> 05:01.390
"Stay flamin"'.

05:01.474 --> 05:04.018
Greetings, my good Hotman.

05:04.101 --> 05:05.895
Oh, hi...

05:05.978 --> 05:08.314
I guess?

05:08.397 --> 05:10.316
AANG: Oh, we're going
to a meat place?

05:10.399 --> 05:13.653
SOKKA: Come on, Aang,
everyone here eats meat...

05:13.736 --> 05:14.862
Even the meat.

05:14.946 --> 05:17.114
( GROWLS )

05:17.198 --> 05:18.533
You guys go ahead.

05:18.616 --> 05:20.743
I'll just get some lettuce
out of the garbage.

05:25.206 --> 05:27.124
AANG: Hotman, Hotman.

05:27.208 --> 05:29.001
Hotman.

05:29.085 --> 05:30.795
Hotman, Hotman.

05:31.629 --> 05:33.422
It's over,
we caught you.

05:33.548 --> 05:34.882
Who me?

05:34.966 --> 05:37.426
It couldn't be more obvious
that you don't belong here.

05:38.427 --> 05:39.679
Next time you play hooky

05:39.804 --> 05:42.557
You might want to take off
your school uniform.

05:43.391 --> 05:45.852
( NERVOUS CHUCKLE ) Ah!

05:55.319 --> 05:56.821
Oh...

05:56.904 --> 05:59.615
TEACHER: Is this a new mind
ready for molding?

05:59.699 --> 06:00.741
That's right.

06:00.825 --> 06:02.869
Let the molding begin.

06:02.952 --> 06:04.036
TEACHER: Wait a minute.

06:04.120 --> 06:06.664
( GASPS ) You're not
from the Fire Nation.

06:09.542 --> 06:11.586
Clearly you're
from the colonies.

06:12.086 --> 06:15.298
Yeah, the colonies,
of course.

06:15.381 --> 06:18.426
The Fire Nation colonies
in the Earth Kingdom.

06:18.509 --> 06:20.469
Your etiquette
is terrible.

06:20.553 --> 06:22.430
In the homeland,
we bow to our elders...

06:23.890 --> 06:26.309
Like so.

06:26.392 --> 06:27.643
Sorry ma'am.

06:33.441 --> 06:36.319
And we don't wear
head coverings indoors.

06:36.402 --> 06:38.487
Um, I have a scar.

06:38.738 --> 06:40.239
It's really embarrassing.

06:40.448 --> 06:41.449
Very well.

06:41.532 --> 06:43.451
What is your name?

06:43.534 --> 06:47.121
Or should we just call you
mannerless colony slob?

06:47.204 --> 06:48.331
( CHUCKLES )

06:48.414 --> 06:49.874
Just "slob" is fine.

06:50.583 --> 06:52.501
Or, uh... Kuzon.

06:56.047 --> 06:57.715
( BELL TOLLS )

06:57.798 --> 07:01.969
( STUDENTS TALKING )

07:04.305 --> 07:05.306
( MOMO PURRS )

07:05.556 --> 07:07.183
We made it through
the day, Momo...

07:07.266 --> 07:08.434
And it was pretty fun.

07:08.517 --> 07:09.810
( PURRS )

07:09.894 --> 07:11.270
Don't let the headmaster
catch you with that monkey.

07:11.812 --> 07:13.022
What monkey?

07:13.105 --> 07:15.358
Don't worry,
I'm not a tattletale.

07:15.441 --> 07:16.442
My name's On Ji.

07:16.525 --> 07:18.110
I like your headband,
by the way.

07:20.071 --> 07:22.657
On ji, you don't have
to baby-sit the new kid.

07:22.740 --> 07:24.575
Wow.

07:24.784 --> 07:27.286
You must be one of those popular
kids I've been hearing about.

07:27.495 --> 07:28.496
That's right.

07:28.579 --> 07:29.664
Now listen, friend...

07:29.747 --> 07:31.248
I know you're from the colonies

07:31.332 --> 07:32.750
so I'll say this slowly.

07:32.917 --> 07:36.087
On Ji is my girlfriend.

07:36.212 --> 07:38.047
Don't forget it.

07:44.679 --> 07:46.263
It was nice meeting you.

07:46.347 --> 07:47.473
I don't believe it.

07:47.556 --> 07:48.557
He didn't beat you up.

07:48.891 --> 07:50.142
Not even a little.

07:50.226 --> 07:51.811
I guess I'm just lucky.

07:51.894 --> 07:53.813
We were on our way to play
hide and explode.

07:53.896 --> 07:54.981
You wanna come?

07:55.064 --> 07:56.399
I'd love to.

08:01.988 --> 08:04.240
KATARA: Where have you been?

08:04.323 --> 08:05.741
We've been worried sick.

08:05.825 --> 08:07.576
I got invited to play
with some kids after school.

08:09.453 --> 08:10.746
SOKKA: After what?

08:11.122 --> 08:13.082
I enrolled in
a Fire Nation school

08:13.165 --> 08:14.583
And I'm going back tomorrow.

08:14.917 --> 08:17.253
Enrolled in what?

08:26.137 --> 08:27.221
You again?

08:27.304 --> 08:29.515
Stop where you are.

08:30.141 --> 08:32.435
GUARD: Prince Zuko?

08:32.518 --> 08:33.519
( SWORD CLANKS )

08:33.602 --> 08:34.979
Ah!

08:35.062 --> 08:36.731
I'm going in for a visit.

08:36.814 --> 08:38.149
You're gonna stand guard here

08:38.232 --> 08:41.444
and no one is going
to know about this.

08:50.119 --> 08:51.162
( DOOR CREAKS OPEN )

08:53.956 --> 08:56.917
Uncle... It's me.

09:07.803 --> 09:11.474
Aang, I'm trying to be mature and not
immediately shoot down your idea.

09:11.599 --> 09:14.143
But it sounds...
Really terrible.

09:14.268 --> 09:16.145
Yeah, we got our outfits.

09:16.270 --> 09:18.439
What do you need
to go to school for?

09:18.564 --> 09:20.441
Every minute
I'm in that classroom

09:20.566 --> 09:22.651
I'm learning new things
about the Fire Nation.

09:22.735 --> 09:24.862
I already have a picture
of Fire Lord, Ozai.

09:25.738 --> 09:27.615
And here's one that
I made out of noodles.

09:27.740 --> 09:29.700
Impressive, I admit.

09:29.825 --> 09:31.368
But I still think
it's too dangerous.

09:31.494 --> 09:35.247
I guess we'll never find out
about the secret river, then.

09:35.372 --> 09:38.250
It goes right to
the Fire Lord's palace.

09:38.375 --> 09:41.253
We were supposed to learn
about it in class tomorrow...

09:41.378 --> 09:45.925
Hmm... I am a fan
of secret rivers.

09:46.050 --> 09:48.511
Fine, let's stay
a few more days.

09:48.636 --> 09:50.513
Flamey-O, Hotman.

09:52.765 --> 09:55.601
- Flamey-O?
-( SHRUGS ) Um-um.

09:57.603 --> 09:59.605
ZUKO: You brought this
on yourself, you know.

09:59.730 --> 10:01.357
We could have returned together.

10:01.482 --> 10:02.483
You could have been a hero.

10:04.902 --> 10:06.946
You had no right
to judge me, Uncle.

10:07.071 --> 10:09.907
I did what I had to do
in Ba Sing Se

10:10.032 --> 10:11.283
and you're a fool
for not joining me.

10:13.661 --> 10:17.248
You're not
gonna say anything?

10:17.373 --> 10:18.415
Oh!

10:18.541 --> 10:20.167
( YELLS )

10:20.292 --> 10:22.336
You're a crazy old man.

10:22.461 --> 10:24.421
You're crazy,
and if you weren't in jail

10:24.547 --> 10:27.174
you'd be sleeping
in a gutter.

10:32.680 --> 10:34.557
TEACHER: Good morning, class.

10:36.225 --> 10:37.309
Recite the Fire Nation oath.

10:38.894 --> 10:41.313
STUDENTS: My life,
I give to my country.

10:41.438 --> 10:42.773
With my hands,
I fight for Fire Lord...

10:42.898 --> 10:44.567
AANG: Fire Lord...

10:44.692 --> 10:46.235
Forefathers...

10:46.360 --> 10:48.612
STUDENTS: With my mind, I seek
ways to better my country

10:48.737 --> 10:50.281
and with my feet...

10:50.406 --> 10:51.490
AANG: Firebenders...

10:51.574 --> 10:53.367
Fire Lord.

10:53.492 --> 10:55.786
- Wha, bah, blah, blah.
-( STUDENTS CHUCKLING )

11:00.791 --> 11:04.336
Since it's obviously hilarious
to mock our national oath

11:04.420 --> 11:07.006
we'll begin with a pop quiz on
our great march of civilization.

11:07.089 --> 11:09.800
( STUDENTS GROAN )

11:10.384 --> 11:12.428
TEACHER: Question one.

11:12.511 --> 11:15.306
What year did Fire Lord Sozin
battle the Air Nation army?

11:18.142 --> 11:19.602
Kuzon?

11:19.727 --> 11:21.604
AANG: Is that a trick question?

11:21.729 --> 11:24.773
The air nomads didn't
have a formal military.

11:24.899 --> 11:28.944
Sozin defeated them by ambush.

11:29.069 --> 11:30.738
TEACHER: Well, I don't know how you could

11:30.821 --> 11:32.865
possibly know more than our
national history book

11:32.990 --> 11:35.701
unless you were there
a hundred years ago.

11:35.826 --> 11:37.411
I'll just write down
my best guess.

11:42.583 --> 11:45.419
( ORCHESTRA PLAYS )

11:45.544 --> 11:48.839
( PLAYS WRONG NOTES )

11:50.716 --> 11:52.009
MUSIC TEACHER: Kuzon?

11:52.092 --> 11:53.093
( STOPS PLAYING )

11:53.177 --> 11:57.056
I know, I'm a terrible
tsungi hornist.

11:57.181 --> 11:58.224
No, child.

11:58.349 --> 12:00.142
That hullabaloo going
on with your feet.

12:00.267 --> 12:02.269
Is that a nervous disorder?

12:02.394 --> 12:05.105
I was just dancing.

12:05.231 --> 12:07.316
You do dances here in the
homeland, right?

12:07.441 --> 12:09.652
Not really, no.

12:09.777 --> 12:13.489
Dancing is not conducive to
a proper learning environment.

12:13.614 --> 12:16.408
Young people must have rigid
discipline and order.

12:16.533 --> 12:18.535
AANG: But what about
expressing yourself?

12:18.661 --> 12:21.372
I know sometimes we're so moved
by our love for our nation

12:21.497 --> 12:25.251
that we can't control
our own bodies.

12:25.376 --> 12:27.127
If you must

12:27.253 --> 12:31.882
you may march in place quietly
next time the urge hits you.

12:32.007 --> 12:34.843
( MUSIC RESUMES )

12:41.767 --> 12:46.605
( ALL TALKING/WHISPERING )

12:46.730 --> 12:49.275
Oh, hi, Kuzon.

12:49.400 --> 12:51.944
I really liked that crazy
dance you were doing.

12:52.069 --> 12:53.153
Thanks, On Ji.

12:53.279 --> 12:54.780
I could show it to you
again if you'd like.

12:54.905 --> 12:55.948
Ah!

12:56.073 --> 12:57.741
What'd you say,
colony trash?

12:57.866 --> 12:59.535
You're gonna show her something?

12:59.660 --> 13:01.245
Just some
dance movements.

13:01.370 --> 13:03.247
Nobody shows
my On Ji anything

13:03.372 --> 13:05.165
Especially movement.

13:05.291 --> 13:06.292
( GRUNTS )

13:07.710 --> 13:09.378
( GRUNTS )

13:09.920 --> 13:12.423
( AUDIBLE STRUGGLING )

13:17.177 --> 13:18.178
Ah!

13:19.722 --> 13:20.723
Ha!

13:21.557 --> 13:22.558
Yah!

13:22.766 --> 13:23.851
Ah.

13:25.477 --> 13:26.854
( GRUNTS )

13:31.400 --> 13:34.194
( SNIFFLES )

13:34.278 --> 13:37.031
Picking fights
on your second day?

13:37.114 --> 13:39.408
We need to have a conference
to discuss your punishment.

13:39.491 --> 13:41.201
Bring your parents
to my office after school.

13:41.660 --> 13:43.412
Parents, but...

13:43.537 --> 13:44.663
Don't be late.

13:53.881 --> 13:56.008
Thank you for coming

13:56.091 --> 13:57.092
Mr. And Mrs...

13:57.176 --> 13:59.762
Fire... Wang Fire.

13:59.845 --> 14:02.222
This is my wife,
Sapphire.

14:02.306 --> 14:04.183
Sapphire Fire,
nice to meet you.

14:04.391 --> 14:06.894
Mr. And Mrs. Fire...

14:06.977 --> 14:09.063
Your son has been enrolled
here for two days

14:09.146 --> 14:10.939
and he's already
causing problems.

14:11.023 --> 14:12.316
He's argued with
his history teacher

14:12.399 --> 14:14.068
disrupted music class

14:14.151 --> 14:15.819
and roughed up my star pupil.

14:16.111 --> 14:17.571
My goodness.

14:17.654 --> 14:19.156
That doesn't sound
like our Kuzon.

14:19.448 --> 14:21.200
That's what any mother
would say, ma'am.

14:21.283 --> 14:23.243
Nonetheless,
you're forewarned.

14:23.327 --> 14:25.245
If he acts up
one more time

14:25.329 --> 14:27.331
I'll have him sent
to reform school...

14:27.414 --> 14:30.042
By which I mean the coal mines.

14:30.125 --> 14:31.168
Are we clear?

14:31.418 --> 14:33.629
Don't you worry,
Mr. Headmaster

14:33.712 --> 14:36.465
I'll straighten this boy
out something fierce.

14:36.548 --> 14:37.758
Young man, as son as we get home,

14:37.841 --> 14:40.010
you're gonna get the punishment of
a lifetime.

14:40.094 --> 14:42.471
That's what I like to hear.

14:48.185 --> 14:50.938
MAI: Orange is such
an awful color.

14:51.021 --> 14:52.606
( SNICKERS )

14:52.689 --> 14:54.900
You're so beautiful
when you hate the world.

14:54.983 --> 14:56.110
I don't hate you.

14:56.193 --> 14:58.904
I don't hate you, too.

14:59.196 --> 15:01.115
( AZULA CLEARS THROAT )

15:01.365 --> 15:04.118
Zuko, could I have
a word with you?

15:04.201 --> 15:07.287
Can't you see we're busy?

15:07.371 --> 15:11.750
Oh, Mai, Ty Lee needs your help
untangling her braid.

15:11.834 --> 15:14.128
Sounds pretty serious.

15:19.925 --> 15:23.846
So I hear you've been to visit your
Uncle Fatso in the prison tower.

15:24.096 --> 15:26.181
That guard told you.

15:26.265 --> 15:29.184
No, you did... Just now.

15:29.393 --> 15:32.271
OK, you caught me.

15:32.354 --> 15:34.106
What is it that
you want, Azula.

15:34.189 --> 15:36.483
Actually, nothing.

15:36.567 --> 15:39.528
Believe it or not,
I'm looking out for you.

15:39.611 --> 15:41.655
If people find out
you've been to see Uncle

15:41.738 --> 15:44.241
they'll think you're
plotting with him.

15:44.324 --> 15:47.453
Just be careful dum-dum.

15:49.913 --> 15:51.665
( BIRDS SQUAWK )

15:51.748 --> 15:52.791
That settles it.

15:52.875 --> 15:54.835
No more school for you,
young man.

15:54.918 --> 15:55.919
AANG: I'm not
ready to leave.

15:56.378 --> 15:58.213
I'm having fun for once

15:58.297 --> 16:00.132
Just being a normal kid.

16:00.215 --> 16:02.468
You don't know
what it's like, Sokka.

16:02.551 --> 16:04.052
You get to be normal
all the time.

16:04.261 --> 16:06.472
Ha, ha.

16:06.555 --> 16:09.516
Listen, guys, those kids at school are
the future of the Fire Nation.

16:09.600 --> 16:11.894
If we wanna change
this place for the better

16:12.102 --> 16:14.438
We need to show them
a little taste of freedom.

16:14.521 --> 16:18.358
What could you possibly do for a country
of depraved little fire monsters?

16:18.442 --> 16:21.320
I'm gonna throw them
a secret dance party.

16:21.403 --> 16:23.780
Go to your room.

16:34.082 --> 16:36.627
I can't believe we're
having a dance party.

16:36.752 --> 16:38.253
It seems so... Silly.

16:38.378 --> 16:40.506
Don't think of it
as a dance party

16:40.631 --> 16:43.842
But as a cultural event
celebrating the art of fancy footwork.

16:46.220 --> 16:47.346
They're coming.

16:47.471 --> 16:49.640
Everyone stop bending.

16:49.765 --> 16:51.475
AANG: Sorry, buddy.

16:51.600 --> 16:53.769
You should probably
wait out back.

16:53.894 --> 16:56.188
( GROWLS )

16:56.313 --> 16:59.066
AANG: I know, you've got
fancier feet than anybody...

16:59.191 --> 17:00.984
And six of 'em.

17:04.988 --> 17:07.366
( MUSIC PLAYS )

17:09.576 --> 17:11.828
AANG: Ladies and gentlemen.

17:11.954 --> 17:14.498
The Flamey-Os!

17:14.623 --> 17:18.001
Yeah, this ought to get
everybody moving.

17:20.504 --> 17:23.131
Now what
do we do?

17:23.257 --> 17:25.342
This is when you start dancing.

17:25.467 --> 17:28.762
I don't think my parents want me
dancing in a cave.

17:28.887 --> 17:32.349
Yeah, what if someone
finds out?

17:32.516 --> 17:33.600
Oh, boy.

17:33.725 --> 17:34.977
Listen, guys...

17:35.102 --> 17:37.312
Dancing isn't something
you think about.

17:37.437 --> 17:39.147
It's a form of self-expression

17:39.273 --> 17:41.483
that no one can ever
take away from you.

17:41.608 --> 17:45.195
Maybe it was different in the colonies,
Kuzon, but we don't do that here.

17:45.279 --> 17:46.280
Sure you do.

17:46.363 --> 17:48.740
You have for generations.

17:48.865 --> 17:51.618
It just so happens that I know
several classic Fire Nation dances.

17:51.743 --> 17:53.662
A hundred years ago

17:53.787 --> 17:55.122
this was known as
"The Phoenix Flight."

17:55.247 --> 17:57.374
STUDENTS: Ooh... Wow.

17:57.499 --> 18:00.502
And this was
the "Camelephant Strut".

18:03.338 --> 18:05.299
( GIGGLING )

18:07.884 --> 18:09.011
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

18:09.136 --> 18:12.222
Who knew Twinkle Toes
could dance?

18:12.347 --> 18:13.724
( CHEERING CONTINUES )

18:15.559 --> 18:17.978
I brought you some
komodo-chicken.

18:18.103 --> 18:19.688
I know you don't care for it

18:19.813 --> 18:22.065
but I figure
it beats prison food.

18:22.190 --> 18:23.317
I admit it.

18:23.442 --> 18:25.694
I have everything
I always wanted

18:25.819 --> 18:28.030
but it's not at all how
I thought it would be.

18:28.155 --> 18:30.574
The truth is

18:30.699 --> 18:32.784
I need your advice.

18:32.909 --> 18:35.996
I think the Avatar
is still alive.

18:36.121 --> 18:37.956
I know he's out there.

18:38.081 --> 18:40.792
I'm losing my mind.

18:40.917 --> 18:44.004
Please, Uncle, I'm so confused,
I need your help.

18:46.173 --> 18:47.507
Forget it.

18:47.633 --> 18:48.884
I'll solve this myself.

18:49.009 --> 18:50.927
Waste away in here
for all I care.

18:55.557 --> 18:57.392
( DOOR CREAKS SHUT )

19:01.938 --> 19:04.775
( DANCE MUSIC CONTINUES )

19:04.900 --> 19:07.694
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

19:09.404 --> 19:11.573
And this is how they do it in
the ballrooms of Ba Sing Se.

19:18.497 --> 19:20.499
Wow, they look pretty
good together.

19:20.624 --> 19:23.293
Eh, if that's what you like.

19:25.170 --> 19:26.254
AANG: Yeah, that's it.

19:26.380 --> 19:29.257
That's the sound of happy feet.

19:33.679 --> 19:35.138
All right, go with that.

19:35.263 --> 19:36.973
Everybody, freestyle.

19:54.366 --> 19:55.826
I don't know, Aang.

19:55.951 --> 19:58.036
These shoes aren't
really right for dancing

19:58.161 --> 20:00.205
and I'm not sure
that I know how to...

20:00.330 --> 20:01.331
Take my hand.

20:01.665 --> 20:02.791
OK.

20:24.062 --> 20:25.897
Aang, everyone's watching.

20:26.022 --> 20:27.232
Don't worry about them.

20:27.357 --> 20:29.860
It's just you and me right now.

20:54.801 --> 20:56.386
( STUDENTS GASP )

20:56.511 --> 20:58.221
STUDENT: Wow.

21:07.939 --> 21:09.441
-( MUSIC ENDS )
-( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

21:09.566 --> 21:12.027
( PANTING )

21:12.152 --> 21:13.320
( FAINT CHEERING )

21:13.445 --> 21:16.281
It is a dancing party.

21:16.406 --> 21:18.492
You did the right thing by
telling me, Hide.

21:18.617 --> 21:20.118
Anytime,
Headmaster, sir.

21:21.578 --> 21:23.663
This is incredible.

21:23.789 --> 21:25.957
It's like my inhibitions
just disappear.

21:31.129 --> 21:34.216
OK, they're back again.

21:34.341 --> 21:35.342
HEADMASTER: He's
the one we want.

21:35.550 --> 21:38.428
The boy with the headband.

21:38.553 --> 21:39.554
Uh-oh.

21:45.018 --> 21:46.061
GUARD: Got ya.

21:46.186 --> 21:47.395
Looking for me?

21:49.064 --> 21:50.440
That's not the one.

21:50.565 --> 21:52.150
He's here somewhere.

21:52.275 --> 21:53.443
Don't let him leave the cave.

21:58.532 --> 21:59.533
Yes?

22:04.287 --> 22:05.914
- Hi there.
- How we doing?

22:13.255 --> 22:14.256
Looking for someone?

22:16.424 --> 22:17.509
Who are you
looking for?

22:17.592 --> 22:18.885
Do you need something?

22:19.010 --> 22:20.011
Over here.

22:33.608 --> 22:36.528
Stop that.

22:36.653 --> 22:37.654
Stop that.

22:40.407 --> 22:42.367
We're safe, Sokka.

22:42.450 --> 22:43.994
You can take off
the mustache, now.

22:44.077 --> 22:45.829
Oh, no, I can't.

22:45.912 --> 22:48.290
It's permanently
glued to my skin.

22:48.373 --> 22:50.750
Way to go, dancy pants.

22:50.834 --> 22:53.086
I think you really
did help those kids.

22:53.211 --> 22:54.588
You taught them to be free.

22:54.671 --> 22:55.672
I don't know.

22:55.755 --> 22:57.632
It was just
a dance party, that's all.

22:57.716 --> 23:00.218
Well, that was some
dance party, Aang.

23:00.844 --> 23:02.137
Mwah.

23:03.680 --> 23:04.973
Flamey-O, sir...

23:05.098 --> 23:06.808
Flamey-O.

23:12.522 --> 23:15.400
( BIRDS CAWING )

23:17.485 --> 23:18.862
( GATE OPENS )

23:20.864 --> 23:22.490
You're sure
you weren't followed?

23:22.616 --> 23:24.784
ZUKO: I've heard about you.

23:24.910 --> 23:27.120
They say you're good
at what you do

23:27.245 --> 23:29.539
and even better
at keeping secrets.

23:29.664 --> 23:31.958
The Avatar's alive.

23:32.083 --> 23:34.169
I want you to find him

23:34.294 --> 23:36.046
and end him.

23:49.392 --> 23:53.229
( ♪... )
